        <h1><a href="http://philbencomo.com/2011/05/the_shard">The Shard</a></h1>
        <p>I heard him, just barely, calling from amid a pile of the dead. His legs were gone, his arms in tatters, and he had not even the strength to open his eyes.</p>

<p>Clutching the trembling remains of a hand, I leaned in close. There was nothing to be done but provide a little comfort and carry on the final words of this dying warrior.</p>

<p>They came slowly, the words, raspy and desiccated between woeful moans.</p>

<p>&#8220;We have dealt a terrible blow, but &#8230; there is &#8230;&#8221; &#8212; whispers now &#8212; &#8220;another &#8230; crystal shard.&#8221;</p>

<p>And then death took him, and it would soon claim our world as well, unless someone among us could find the shard and restore THE DARK CRYSTAL.</p>

